{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"value"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"title":"value","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLAccidentalV5valueAA0C5ValueOvp","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidental\/value"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidental\/value","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidental"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value of this element."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"title":"MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","abstract":[{"text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidental/value":{"title":"value","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidental\/value","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The value of this element.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidentalValue","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidental\/value"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidental":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental type represents actual notated accidentals. Editorial and cautionary indications are indicated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by attributes. Values for these attributes are “no” if not present. Specific graphic display such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parentheses, brackets, and size are controlled by the level-display attribute group."}],"title":"MXLAccidental","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLAccidental","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLAccidental","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidental","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidental"}}}